00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:28,790
So now probably a lot of you have an idea of what it means to be a vegetarian, but let's take a look at that word and many more on Language Takeaway.

30
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:31,860
Language Takeaway.

31
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:36,660
So a vegetarian is a noun.

32
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:39,280
I am a vegetarian.

33
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,280
Yeah.

34
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:41,280
Vegetarian is a noun.

35
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,720
It's a person.

36
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,220
You say I am a vegetarian.

37
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:46,020
He is a vegetarian.

38
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:54,120
And in this case, a vegetarian person does not eat meat.

39
00:01:54,170 --> 00:01:57,370
So no chicken, no beef, none of that stuff.

40
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:58,170
That's right.

41
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,960
So as you can see, it has the prefix veget, like vegetable.

42
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:04,960
So that's what they eat.

43
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:05,650
They just eat vegetables.

44
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:16,260
And it's a little bit hard to say what all vegetarians do or don't eat because some people have different rules.

45
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:16,980
That's right.

46
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:19,040
Some people eat eggs, some people don't.

47
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:22,340
But there is something that is a little bit different from a vegetarian.

48
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:27,720
It's called a vegan and this person has many, many rules about what he can or cannot eat.

49
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:28,360
Right.

50
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,520
So a vegetarian basically does not eat meat.

51
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:44,240
A vegan, as we saw in our dialogue, doesn't wear leather, for example, doesn't wear leather shoes or a jacket or use or eat anything that comes from an animal.

52
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:45,140
That's right.

53
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:46,800
No eggs, right?

54
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:51,780
No foods that might have any animal products in them.

55
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:59,480
So vegans often try to find foods at the grocery store that come from natural products that are not animal based.

56
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:06,080
And so there has to be a symbol on the back of the box or the jar that says that it's vegan.

57
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,080
That's right.

58
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:12,680
So in that case, they don't drink milk, they don't eat eggs, nothing that you can think of that comes from an animal.

59
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:17,560
But on the other hand, this person used to be a pescatarian.

60
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:22,540
So this is another type of person that has a special diet, very much like a vegetarian.

61
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:28,880
A pescatarian is a person who is a vegetarian but who also eats fish.

62
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:34,360
And so maybe I'm a pescatarian because I don't consider fish to be animals.

63
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:35,360
Okay.

64
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:38,800
So I don't eat lamb, I don't eat chicken, but I do eat fish.

65
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:39,800
I'm a pescatarian.

66
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:40,800
All right.

67
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:55,760
So a vegetarian does not eat fish or any type of meat, the same as a vegan, but a pescatarian does eat maybe shrimp and fish and any type of animal from the sea.

68
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:56,760
Okay.

69
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:58,840
And well, that brings us up to our next word.

70
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:00,820
A pescatarian will eat seafood.

71
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:05,900
Seafood is a word we use to describe animals that come from the sea.

72
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:07,200
So not just fish.

73
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:11,640
So like you said, shrimp and lobster.

74
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:19,120
You could even think of really delicious food like a seafood pasta or a seafood salad, octopus, things like that.

75
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,120
Okay.

76
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:24,240
So you got clams, you have oysters, anything that comes from the sea is considered seafood.

77
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:24,560
Right?

78
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,240
That's right.

79
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:28,920
And our last word in language takeaway is an adjective.

80
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:33,880
We heard at the end of the dialogue, our character said, it must be tough.

81
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:34,880
Right.

82
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:35,880
Okay.

83
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:42,680
That's an interesting word because in English it has a few different meanings, but what was the meaning of the word tough in today's dialogue?

84
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:48,420
In today's dialogue, when the person said it must be tough, it's basically saying it must be difficult.

85
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:51,200
It must be difficult to be a vegetarian.

86
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:52,280
Right.

87
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,440
So it's a hard situation.

88
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:57,460
You could also say, oh man, this homework is really tough.

89
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:58,900
That means it's hard.

90
00:04:59,280 --> 00:04:59,560
It's difficult.

91
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,280
All right.

