00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:13,160
Fluency Builder.

120
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:20,860
So there's a very interesting and very, very common phrase at the beginning of today's dialogue that we use all the time in English.

121
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:23,600
This is to grab something to eat.

122
00:06:24,020 --> 00:06:27,500
The character says, hey Julie, you want to go grab something to eat?

123
00:06:27,860 --> 00:06:33,220
So taking that as a phrase, we are inviting someone to go eat something.

124
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:34,060
That's right.

125
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:37,680
So I could say, hey, do you want to go eat something?

126
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:42,010
Or I could say, hey, do you want to go grab something to eat?

127
00:06:42,410 --> 00:06:42,610
Okay.

128
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:46,880
And the verb grab is to take or to hold in your hand.

129
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:50,120
So you want to go grab something to eat is basically that.

130
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:50,390
Right.

131
00:06:50,550 --> 00:06:59,250
But don't be confused because grabbing normally means holding with your hand, but to grab something to eat generally just means, hey, would you like to go eat something with me?

132
00:06:59,510 --> 00:06:59,810
Okay.

133
00:07:00,190 --> 00:07:07,820
And of course we want to go grab something to eat and the guy says, I really feel like having a big juicy steak.

134
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:12,160
So we feel like having a steak.

135
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:13,500
This is very spoken English.

136
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:18,520
So remember when you're talking to your friends, this is okay, but maybe if you're writing something it's not as good.

137
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:23,420
But I feel like a steak means I want to eat a steak.

138
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:24,680
Right.

139
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:25,680
So you're saying you are a steak.

140
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:32,200
No, I don't feel like a steak, like a piece of meat, but I do want to eat a piece of, I do want to eat a steak.

141
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:35,320
And so I feel like having, or I feel like a steak.

142
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:37,380
These are both acceptable in spoken English.

143
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:42,760
So you basically feel like doing something or you feel like eating something.

144
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:47,910
For example, if we're going to have dinner, you can say, I feel like having Italian food.

145
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:49,560
Yeah.

146
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,360
