148
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:54,820
And I also feel like watching a movie.

149
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,200
Exactly.

150
00:07:56,200 --> 00:08:01,300
So great ways of using feel like, and then a verb like having or watching a movie.

151
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:14,200
Now getting back to the vegetarian, the vegan aspect of our dialogue, we saw that the girl explained how she doesn't eat or use any animal based products.

152
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:17,540
So these three words, animal based products.

153
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:22,020
So product is basically anything that will be sold or bought.

154
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,340
Animal based is a way to describe a product.

155
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:29,760
So some products have animal products in them.

156
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:36,600
So for example, my shoes are an animal based product because they are leather and leather comes from cows, which are animals.

157
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:40,340
So you're basically saying that they have something from an animal.

158
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:44,960
They are made up of something that comes from an animal like leather shoes.

159
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:45,840
Exactly.

160
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,120
And it's not just shoes.

161
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:52,540
It's also shampoo or some of the foods that you eat like in jars and cans.

162
00:08:53,840 --> 00:09:00,560
It's important if you're a vegan to look on the side of the can or the side of the box and see is this an animal based product?

163
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:03,600
Are there animal products in this?

164
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,600
Right.

165
